atem:
  line: A single-file Python library that parses malformed, often machine-written XML without failing, as a stream
    of events or an ElementTree.
  focus: It trades XML compliance for resilience, repairing broken tags, attributes, entities, comments and CDATA
    as it goes. Every repair can be reported as a ParseError event with its line and column.
  push: Code that must read XML a language model wrote, where a strict parser would stop at the first mistake.
  pull: It deliberately is not a conforming XML parser, and its own author says he cannot vouch for its quality.
