- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.tree_parse.doc
  type: behaviour
  name: What the docstring of tree_parse says
  summary: The docstring of tree_parse of sloppy_xml, as written.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.tree_parse
  when: tree_parse is used
  does: "Build XML tree from input or parsing events.\n\nThis is a convenience function that combines streaming\
    \ parsing with tree\nbuilding. It can accept either raw XML input (which will be parsed) or\nan iterator of\
    \ parsing events.\n\nArgs:\n    xml_input: XML string, file-like object, or iterator of XMLEvents\n    tree_builder:\
    \ Tree builder instance (defaults to ElementTreeBuilder)\n    **parse_options: Options passed to stream_parse\
    \ if needed\n\nReturns:\n    ET.Element: Root element of the constructed XML tree\n\nRaises:\n    ValueError:\
    \ If input is invalid or tree construction fails\n    TypeError: If tree_builder doesn't implement TreeBuilder\
    \ interface\n\nExamples:\n    >>> xml = \"<root><child>text</child></root>\"\n    >>> root = tree_parse(xml)\n\
    \    >>> root.tag\n    'root'\n    >>> root[0].text\n    'text'\n\n    >>> # Use enhanced options for fragments\n\
    \    >>> root = tree_parse(\"text only\", allow_fragments=True)"
