- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.events-are-tuples
  type: behaviour
  name: Parsing events are named tuples
  summary: The parser reports what it finds as seven kinds of immutable named-tuple events, together the type XMLEvent.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.StartElement
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.EndElement
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.Text
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.Comment
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ProcessingInstruction
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.EntityRef
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ParseError
  - C:component/sloppy_xml
  when: stream_parse yields an event
  does: Each event is a typing.NamedTuple with exactly the fields listed in its structure, in that order, so it
    compares equal to a plain tuple of the same values and unpacks positionally. Every event carries the line and
    column where it was found in the source.
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 71-135
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L71-L135
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2238-edda
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1
  ruling:
  - is: alike
    allowing: own-types
    because: the target's own types
    made-for: N:target/rust
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-18'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q1: as proposed: the driver contract is the kept interface, ruled changed for Rust (it ships
      sloppy-cases); the Python API alike, made-for rust; sitting 2: a fifth allowance, own-types, on the closed
      list: a value may take the target''s own type where the kept interface cannot see the difference'
    about: S-R22
  - is: kept
    about: the rest of the behaviour
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: '5d Q-D1: ruled as proposed, in one batch: every pending item takes the worksheet''s proposal (sections
      1 and 2''s last column); the owner may overrule any one later'
  - is: kept
    because: the round trip carries the original as recorded
    about: S-R22
    made-for: N:target/python
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: '5d Q-D2: every other item is kept for the round trip, as recorded'
- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.lxml-optional
  type: behaviour
  name: lxml is optional
  summary: The module imports lxml.etree if it can and records whether it could in HAS_LXML.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:component/sloppy_xml
  when: the module is imported
  does: Tries "from lxml import etree as lxml_etree"; on success HAS_LXML is True, on ImportError HAS_LXML is False
    and lxml_etree is None. Only when HAS_LXML is True is LxmlElementTreeBuilder defined, appended to __all__, and
    registered as the "lxml" backend; "etree" (ElementTreeBuilder) is always registered. The backends are kept in
    a module-level dict _backends mapping the names "etree" and "lxml" to builder classes.
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 33-40
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L33-L40
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2238-edda
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1
  ruling:
  - is: alike
    allowing: own-types
    because: an lxml-like builder in Rust's own types
    about: 'S-R20: the builder'
    made-for: N:target/rust
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-18'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q4: alike: Rust offers an lxml-like tree builder of its own under the name lxml, in Rust''s
      own types (tags, attributes, text, tail), printed by the driver like the original''s; sitting 2: a fifth allowance,
      own-types, on the closed list: a value may take the target''s own type where the kept interface cannot see
      the difference'
  - is: alike
    allowing: exit-only
    about: 'S-R20: the refusal of an unknown name'
    made-for: N:target/rust
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q3: alike, exit-only allowed: fails on the same inputs at the same point; the kind need not
      be named in Python''s words'
  - is: kept
