- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.etree-builder
  type: behaviour
  name: Building an ElementTree from events
  summary: ElementTreeBuilder turns the events into an xml.etree.ElementTree tree, keeping a stack of open elements
    and a text buffer.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.__init__
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.start_element
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.end_element
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.text
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.comment
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.processing_instruction
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.entity_ref
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.parse_error
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ElementTreeBuilder.get_root
  when: a tree is built from events
  does: '__init__ sets self.root = None, self.element_stack = [] and self.current_text = [] (a list of strings).
    start_element first flushes the text buffer, creates ET.Element(event.name, event.attrs); the first element
    created becomes root, every later one is appended to the element on top of the stack (if the stack is empty
    it is created but attached nowhere); then it is pushed. end_element flushes the text and pops the stack if it
    is not empty (auto_closed is ignored). text appends event.content to the buffer (CDATA is plain text). entity_ref
    appends event.resolved to the buffer. comment and processing_instruction flush the buffer and keep nothing (ElementTree
    keeps no comments or PIs). parse_error does nothing, fatal or not. get_root flushes the buffer and returns root
    (None if no element was ever started). Flushing (the private _flush_text): if the buffer is empty, clear it
    and stop; otherwise join it; if the joined text is non-empty and the stack is not empty, it goes to the top
    element''s text when that element has no children yet (appended to existing text), else to the tail of its last
    child (appended to an existing tail); text with no open element is dropped; the buffer is cleared.'
  edges:
  - given: text then an entity_ref then text inside one element
    then: the three pieces are joined into one string in the element's text
  - given: text after a child element closed
    then: it becomes that child''s tail
  - given: text before the first element or after the root closed
    then: it is dropped
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 303-436
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L303-L436
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2238-edda
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1
  ruling:
  - is: alike
    allowing: own-types
    because: the target's own tree type, kept at the driver's dump (S-I2)
    made-for: N:target/rust
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-18'
    said: '5d Q-D1: ruled as proposed, in one batch: every pending item takes the worksheet''s proposal (sections
      1 and 2''s last column); the owner may overrule any one later; sitting 2: a fifth allowance, own-types, on
      the closed list: a value may take the target''s own type where the kept interface cannot see the difference'
    about: S-R15
  - is: kept
    about: the rest of the behaviour
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: '5d Q-D1: ruled as proposed, in one batch: every pending item takes the worksheet''s proposal (sections
      1 and 2''s last column); the owner may overrule any one later'
  - is: kept
    because: the round trip carries the original as recorded
    about: S-R15
    made-for: N:target/python
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: '5d Q-D2: every other item is kept for the round trip, as recorded'
- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.lxml-builder
  type: behaviour
  name: Building an lxml tree from events
  summary: LxmlElementTreeBuilder is ElementTreeBuilder with lxml elements, and it keeps comments and processing
    instructions.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.LxmlElementTreeBuilder
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.LxmlElementTreeBuilder.__init__
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.LxmlElementTreeBuilder.start_element
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.LxmlElementTreeBuilder.get_root
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.LxmlElementTreeBuilder.comment
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.LxmlElementTreeBuilder.processing_instruction
  when: tree_parse is asked for the lxml tree and lxml is installed
  does: Subclasses ElementTreeBuilder (end_element, text, entity_ref, parse_error and the text flushing are inherited).
    __init__ calls the parent's and resets root to None and the stack to []. start_element is the parent's with
    lxml_etree.Element(event.name, event.attrs). get_root flushes and returns root. comment flushes and, if an element
    is open, appends lxml_etree.Comment(event.content) to the top element. processing_instruction flushes and, if
    an element is open, appends lxml_etree.ProcessingInstruction(event.target, event.data) to it. A comment or PI
    outside every element is dropped.
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 444-505
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L444-L505
    confidence: 0.9
