- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.stream-input
  type: behaviour
  name: Reading the input
  summary: stream_parse takes a string or anything with read(), decodes bytes, and optionally cleans encoding problems
    before parsing.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: stream_parse(xml_input, ...) is iterated (it is a generator; nothing happens until the first next())
  does: All keyword options are first copied into a _ParseOptions record. If xml_input has a read attribute, text
    = xml_input.read(); bytes are decoded with options.encoding. On UnicodeDecodeError with fix_encoding true, it
    tries read().decode() again with "latin1", "cp1252", then "ascii" (a second read of a consumed stream gives
    what it gives); if none works, or fix_encoding is false, it raises UnicodeDecodeError whose reason is "Unable
    to decode input with {encoding} encoding". Anything without read is turned into text with str(xml_input). Then,
    when fix_encoding is true, the private _fix_encoding_issues(text) returns (fixed text, list of fix messages);
    when emit_errors is true each fix message is yielded at once as a ParseError of error_type "encoding_fix", message
    and recovery the fix message, line 1, column 1, fatal False, severity "warning" (made by the private _create_error_with_context
    with the original text and position 0).
  errors:
  - when: bytes cannot be decoded and no fallback works, or fix_encoding is False
    message: Unable to decode input with {options.encoding} encoding (as the reason of a UnicodeDecodeError)
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
