- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.stream-loop
  type: behaviour
  name: The parsing loop
  summary: stream_parse scans the text from position 0 with the PATTERNS, trying constructs in a fixed order and
    tracking line and column.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: while the position is inside the text
  does: 'State: pos 0, line 1, column 1, a stack of open tag names, a text buffer, a recovery counter and a list
    of collected errors. At each step, first: if the stack is deeper than max_depth, emit the fatal error "depth_exceeded"
    and stop the loop; if the recovery counter exceeds max_recovery_attempts, emit the fatal error "recovery_limit"
    and stop. Then try, in this order, each anchored at pos: (1) comment <!--...--> : flush text, yield Comment(group
    1, line, column); (2) only with recovery_strategy LENIENT or AGGRESSIVE, broken_comment: flush, yield Comment(content),
    then error "broken_comment", counter +1; (3) cdata: flush, yield Text(content, line, column, is_cdata=True);
    (4) LENIENT or AGGRESSIVE only, broken_cdata: flush, yield Text(content, is_cdata=True), error "broken_cdata",
    counter +1; (5) pi <?target data?> : flush, yield ProcessingInstruction(target, data stripped or None when empty,
    line, column); (6) end tag; (7) start tag; (8) text_content [^<&]+ is appended to the buffer; (9) an entity
    reference is appended to the buffer as written (resolved when flushed); (10) LENIENT or AGGRESSIVE only, an
    incomplete tag via the private _handle_incomplete_tag(text, pos, line, column, strategy), which returns (tag
    name or None, new position, messages): flush, yield StartElement(name, {}, line, column, None), and if auto_close_tags
    yield EndElement(name, line, column, auto_closed=True); each message is an "incomplete_tag" error; pos jumps
    to the new position; counter +1; (11) smart_quotes on and LENIENT or AGGRESSIVE and the character is " or '':
    the private _smart_quote_recovery(text, pos) returns (fixed text, new position, messages); if there are messages
    the whole text is replaced by the fixed text, each message is a "quote_mismatch" error, counter +1, and the
    loop goes on at the same pos; (12) otherwise one character is consumed: it is added to the buffer unless it
    is a space, tab, CR or LF and preserve_whitespace is off. After every match, line and column are advanced over
    the matched text by the private _update_position(text, start, end, line, column); a consumed newline adds one
    to line and sets column to 1, any other character adds one to column. Every event carries the line and column
    at the START of what it reports, except Text from the buffer (see flushing).'
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 657-1095
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L657-L1095
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2238-edda
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1
  ruling:
  - is: kept
    because: the behaviour kept; the means free (crates allowed)
    made-for: N:target/rust
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q2: third-party crates allowed, each pinned and named; the behaviour kept'
    about: S-R01
  - is: kept
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: '5d Q-D1: ruled as proposed, in one batch: every pending item takes the worksheet''s proposal (sections
      1 and 2''s last column); the owner may overrule any one later'
    about: S-R19
  - is: kept
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: '5d Q-D1: ruled as proposed, in one batch: every pending item takes the worksheet''s proposal (sections
      1 and 2''s last column); the owner may overrule any one later'
