- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.stream-tags
  type: behaviour
  name: Start and end tags
  summary: stream_parse yields StartElement and EndElement events, pairs a self-closing tag at once, and recovers
    from mismatched end tags.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: a start tag or an end tag is matched
  does: 'End tag </name>: flush the text. If the stack is not empty and its top is not this name: with recover on,
    the private _recover_tag_mismatch(stack, name, line, column) returns a list of events which are all yielded
    (it may change the stack), then the warning "tag_mismatch" with the message "Mismatched end tag ''NAME'', expected
    ''TOP''" (TOP the stack''s top after recovery, or none) and recovery "auto-closed N tags" (N the number of events
    returned), counter +1; with recover off, the fatal error "tag_mismatch" "Mismatched end tag ''NAME''" and the
    loop stops. If the top matches, it is popped. In every case that does not stop, EndElement(name, line, column,
    auto_closed=False) is yielded, also for an end tag with nothing open. Start tag <name attrs> or <name attrs/>:
    flush the text; attributes come from the private _repair_attributes(attr string, smart_quotes, recovery_strategy,
    resolve_entities) when repair_attributes is on (it returns (dict, messages); each message becomes an "attribute_repair"
    warning with message and recovery the message, counter +1 each), else from the private _parse_attributes(attr
    string, resolve_entities); if either raises, attributes are {} and the error "attribute_parse" "Failed to parse
    attributes: {e}" with recovery "using empty attributes". With namespace_aware on and a ":" in the name, namespace
    is the value of the attribute xmlns:PREFIX (PREFIX the part before the first ":"), else None. Yield StartElement(name,
    attributes, line, column, namespace). Not self-closing: push the name. Self-closing: yield EndElement(name,
    L, C, auto_closed=False) at once, where L, C is the position just after the closing "/>" (computed from the
    start of the tag over the whole tag).'
  edges:
  - given: <root><child>text</child></root>
    then: 'StartElement root, StartElement child, Text "text", EndElement child, EndElement root: five events by
      the code as read (the docstring says 4)'
  - given: <a/>
    then: StartElement("a", {}, 1, 1, None) then EndElement("a", 1, 5, False)
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 909-1011
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L909-L1011
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2238-edda
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1
