- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.stream-flush
  type: behaviour
  name: Flushing text
  summary: Text gathered in the buffer becomes one Text event, after whitespace, escaping and entity rules.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: before any comment, CDATA, PI, tag or incomplete tag, and at the end of input
  does: 'If the buffer is empty nothing happens. Otherwise its pieces are joined and the buffer cleared. If normalize_whitespace,
    every run of whitespace becomes one space. If the result is only whitespace (or empty) and preserve_whitespace
    is off, nothing is yielded; the text is NOT stripped otherwise. With LENIENT or AGGRESSIVE: every <, > or &
    that is not inside an entity reference matched by PATTERNS["entity_ref"] is replaced by &lt;, &gt; or &amp;,
    and if anything changed the warning "unescaped_chars" "Fixed N unescaped characters in text" with recovery "escaped
    special characters" is emitted. Then, with resolve_entities on, every entity reference is replaced by the private
    _resolve_entity(name, False) for a named one, _resolve_entity(digits, True) for &#NN;, and _resolve_entity("x"
    + hex digits, True) for &#xHH;; then, with LENIENT or AGGRESSIVE, a semicolon is added after every reference
    PATTERNS["broken_entity"] still finds, with the warning "broken_entity" "Fixed N broken entity references" and
    recovery "added missing semicolons". Finally yield Text(content, line, column, is_cdata=False) where line and
    column are the parser''s position at the moment of the flush, that is just after the text. Entity references
    in text are therefore never yielded as EntityRef events by this loop.'
  edges:
  - given: text "a &amp; b" with resolve_entities on
    then: Text content "a & b"
  - given: whitespace only between two tags, preserve_whitespace off
    then: no Text event
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 685-800
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L685-L800
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2238-edda
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1
  ruling:
  - is: kept
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
