- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.stream-end
  type: behaviour
  name: The end of input
  summary: At the end stream_parse flushes text, closes what is still open, and gives the collected errors.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: the loop ends (input used up, or a fatal stop)
  does: 'Flush the text. If recover and auto_close_tags are on and tags are still open: the warning "unclosed_tags"
    "N unclosed tags at end of input" with recovery "auto-closing all remaining tags", then EndElement(name, line,
    column, auto_closed=True) for each open tag, innermost first, all at the final position. Last, if collect_errors
    is on, every collected ParseError is yielded in the order it arose.'
  edges:
  - given: <root><child>
    then: StartElement root, StartElement child, EndElement child (auto_closed True), EndElement root (auto_closed
      True)
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
