- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.stream-errors
  type: behaviour
  name: Errors as events
  summary: Problems become ParseError events, given at once, collected for the end, or dropped.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.ParseError
  when: the parser meets something it repairs or cannot parse
  does: 'Each error is built by the private _create_error_with_context(error_type, message, line, column, text,
    pos, recovery, fatal, severity) with severity "error" and fatal False unless said otherwise. With collect_errors
    on it is kept and yielded after everything else; else with emit_errors on it is yielded where it arose; else
    it is dropped. The error_type values: encoding_fix, unescaped_chars, broken_entity, depth_exceeded (fatal, "Maximum
    nesting depth {max_depth} exceeded", "stopping parse"), recovery_limit (fatal, "Maximum recovery attempts ({max_recovery_attempts})
    exceeded", "stopping recovery"), broken_comment ("Fixed malformed comment (missing closing -->)", "added missing
    comment close"), broken_cdata ("Fixed malformed CDATA section (missing closing ]]>)", "added missing CDATA close"),
    tag_mismatch, attribute_repair, attribute_parse, incomplete_tag, quote_mismatch, unclosed_tags. Warnings have
    severity "warning"; the fatal ones and attribute_parse have severity "error".'
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 666-683
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L666-L683
    confidence: 0.9
