- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.tree-parse
  type: behaviour
  name: Building a tree
  summary: tree_parse feeds the events of its input to a tree builder and returns the root, or a synthetic fragment
    element when there is none.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.tree_parse
  when: tree_parse(xml_input, tree_builder=None, tree="etree", **parse_options)
  does: 'With no tree_builder, a new builder of the backend named by tree is made: _backends[tree]() ("etree" gives
    ElementTreeBuilder; "lxml" gives LxmlElementTreeBuilder and exists only when lxml is installed, else the lookup
    fails with KeyError). If xml_input is iterable, not a str or bytes, and has no read attribute, it is taken as
    the events themselves; otherwise the events are stream_parse(xml_input, **parse_options). Each event goes to
    the builder method of its type: StartElement to start_element, EndElement to end_element, Text to text, Comment
    to comment, ProcessingInstruction to processing_instruction, EntityRef to entity_ref, ParseError to parse_error;
    anything else is ignored. Then root = builder.get_root(). If root is None: when parse_options.get("allow_fragments",
    True) is true it returns a new empty xml.etree.ElementTree.Element("fragment") (an ElementTree element even
    with the lxml backend); otherwise it raises ValueError("No valid XML root element found"). Else it returns root.'
  edges:
  - given: tree_parse("<root><child>text</child></root>")
    then: root.tag is "root" and root[0].text is "text"
  - given: tree_parse("text only")
    then: an empty element with tag "fragment"
  - given: tree_parse("text only", allow_fragments=False)
    then: 'ValueError: No valid XML root element found'
  errors:
  - when: the builder gives no root and allow_fragments is False
    message: No valid XML root element found
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 1118-1200
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L1118-L1200
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2238-edda
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1
  ruling:
  - is: alike
    allowing: own-types
    because: the target's own tree type, kept at the driver's dump (S-I2)
    made-for: N:target/rust
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-18'
    said: '5d Q-D1: ruled as proposed, in one batch: every pending item takes the worksheet''s proposal (sections
      1 and 2''s last column); the owner may overrule any one later; sitting 2: a fifth allowance, own-types, on
