- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.resolve-entity
  type: behaviour
  name: Resolving one entity
  summary: The private _resolve_entity turns an entity name or number into its character, or gives the reference
    back as written.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: text or an attribute value holds an entity reference and resolve_entities is on
  does: '_resolve_entity(entity_name, is_numeric=False): numeric: a name starting with x or X is hexadecimal after
    that letter, else decimal; a code point from 0 to 0x10FFFF gives chr(code point). Named: the name is looked
    up in HTML_ENTITIES as given, then with ";" added. Anything unresolved (bad digits, out of range, unknown name)
    gives "&" + entity_name + ";". _resolve_entities_in_text(text) returns text unchanged when it is empty or has
    no "&"; otherwise every PATTERNS["entity_ref"] match is replaced: a name by _resolve_entity(name, False), &#NN;
    by _resolve_entity(NN, True), &#xHH; by _resolve_entity("x"+HH, True).'
  edges:
  - given: '&amp;'
    then: '&'
  - given: '&#65;'
    then: A
  - given: '&#x41;'
    then: A
  - given: '&unknown;'
    then: '&unknown;'
  - given: '&#1114112; (above 0x10FFFF)'
    then: '&1114112; (the reference given back without its #)'
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 1208-1285
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
