- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.attributes
  type: behaviour
  name: Parsing attributes
  summary: Attributes are read by PATTERNS["attributes"] into a dict; with repair, leftovers with mixed or missing
    quotes are recovered with messages.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: a start tag has an attribute string
  does: '_parse_attributes(attr_string, resolve_entities=True): an all-whitespace string gives {}; each match of
    PATTERNS["attributes"] gives name and value: the double-quoted value, else the single-quoted one, else the unquoted
    one, else "" for a name without a value; a non-empty value has its entities resolved when resolve_entities;
    a later duplicate name overwrites. _repair_attributes(attr_string, smart_quotes=True, recovery_strategy=LENIENT,
    resolve_entities=True) returns (dict, messages): first exactly as _parse_attributes; then, unless the strategy
    is STRICT, every matched text is removed once from the string and what remains (stripped) is examined: with
    smart_quotes, each PATTERNS["mixed_quotes"] match (name="value'' or name=''value") sets name to its value (entities
    resolved) with the message "Fixed mixed quotes in attribute ''NAME''"; then each PATTERNS["malformed_attr"]
    match sets the value with the message "Added quotes to unquoted attribute ''NAME''".'
  edges:
  - given: a="1" b='2' c=3 d
    then: '{''a'': ''1'', ''b'': ''2'', ''c'': ''3'', ''d'': ''''}'
  - given: x="a &amp; b"
    then: '{''x'': ''a & b''}'
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 1288-1530
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - sloppy_xml.py#L1288-L1530
    confidence: 0.9
