- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.positions
  type: behaviour
  name: Counting lines and columns
  summary: The private _update_position moves a line and column over a stretch of text, with a quirk after a newline.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: the parser consumes a match
  does: '_update_position(text, start, end, line, column): with no newline in text[start:end] it returns (line,
    column + (end - start)); otherwise line plus the number of newlines, and as column the number of characters
    after the last newline (not that number plus one), so a match that crosses a line ends at a column one less
    than counting from 1 would give.'
  edges:
  - given: '"ab" from (1, 1)'
    then: (1, 3)
  - given: '"a\nbc" from (1, 1)'
    then: (2, 2)
  span:
