- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.encoding-fixes
  type: behaviour
  name: Fixing encoding problems
  summary: The private _fix_encoding_issues removes control characters and replaces typographic characters with
    plain ones.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: fix_encoding is on
  does: If PATTERNS["encoding_issues"] finds any of the characters U+0000-U+0008, U+000B, U+000C, U+000E-U+001F,
    U+007F-U+009F, they are all removed and the message "Removed N control characters" is added. Then, in this order,
    en dash U+2013 becomes "-", em dash U+2014 "--", U+2018 and U+2019 become an apostrophe, U+201C and U+201D a
    double quote, ellipsis U+2026 "...", no-break space U+00A0 a space; for each one present the message "Replaced
    'X' with 'Y'" is added (X the character itself).
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 1533-1569
  provenance:
    mode: derived
