- id: C:behaviour/sloppy_xml.incomplete-tags
  type: behaviour
  name: Incomplete tags
  summary: The private _handle_incomplete_tag recovers a tag cut off at the end of input.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/sloppy_xml.stream_parse
  when: nothing else matched at pos
  does: If PATTERNS["incomplete_tag"] (a "<name ..." with no ">" before the end of the text) matches at pos and
    the strategy is LENIENT or AGGRESSIVE, it returns (name, len(text), ["Added missing '>' to incomplete tag 'NAME'"]).
    Else, if the rest of the text stripped starts with "<" and the strategy is AGGRESSIVE and a tag name follows
    the "<", it returns (name, len(text), ["Recovered incomplete tag 'NAME'"]). Otherwise (None, pos, []). Recovering
    jumps to the end of the input.
  edges:
  - given: <root><child
    then: StartElement root, StartElement child, EndElement child (auto_closed True), then root closed at the end
  span:
    file: sloppy_xml.py
    lines: 1616-1662
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
