  summary: Any value has a printed form.
  stance: observed
  'on': language
  gives: Any value has a printed form. Text prints as itself; bytes print as b followed by the quoted bytes; a quoted
    form of text (used in many messages) puts it in single quotes, or double quotes when it holds a single quote
    and no double one, with backslash escapes for what cannot be shown.
