  'on': language
  gives: A map from keys to values holds each key once and keeps the order in which keys were first put in; putting
    a key in again changes its value and keeps its place; a map built from sorted pairs stays sorted. Looking up
    a key it does not hold is refused with a key error unless a default is given.
