- id: C:reliance/error-kinds
  type: reliance
  name: errors caught by kind
  summary: A handler catches the kinds of error it names and every kind made from them.
  stance: observed
  'on': language
  gives: A handler catches the kinds of error it names and every kind made from them. A text that is not valid JSON
    is a kind of value error; a missing key is a key error; a wrong kind of value is usually a type error; a missing
    file, a folder where a file was wanted and a refused permission are kinds of operating-system error.
  example: a line that is not JSON and a line missing a field are both caught by one handler naming value and key
