- id: C:reliance/text-decoding-strict
  type: reliance
  name: text decoded strictly
  summary: Text decoded as UTF-8 refuses the first byte sequence that is not valid UTF-8 with a decoding error,
    a kind of value error, naming the position; a byte-order mark at the start is kept as the character U+FEFF,
    unless the encoding asked for is the one that drops it.
  stance: observed
  'on': runtime
  gives: Text decoded as UTF-8 refuses the first byte sequence that is not valid UTF-8 with a decoding error, a
    kind of value error, naming the position; a byte-order mark at the start is kept as the character U+FEFF, unless
    the encoding asked for is the one that drops it.
  example: a ledger holding the byte 0xE9 alone fails to read; a file beginning with a byte-order mark gives a first
    line that begins with U+FEFF.
