- id: C:reliance/bytes-decoded
  type: reliance
  name: bytes and text are different things
  summary: Bytes and text are different kinds and are never mixed silently.
  stance: observed
  'on': runtime
  gives: Bytes and text are different kinds and are never mixed silently. Bytes become text only by decoding them
    with a named encoding, which fails on bytes that encoding cannot read; text read from a byte file is decoded
    once, and a file already read to its end gives nothing more.
  example: '"<r>é</r>" in Latin-1 bytes, decoded as UTF-8, fails at the é.'
  stated:
