- id: C:reliance/pytest-conventions
  type: reliance
  name: the test runner's own names
  summary: The common test runner calls, without being asked, functions named setup_module, teardown_module, setup_function
    and teardown_function, methods named setup_class, teardown_class, setup_method and teardown_method, functions
    named test_ and classes named Test in files whose names mark them as tests; a program that reports unused code
    must not report them.
  stance: observed
  'on': dependency
  gives: The common test runner calls, without being asked, functions named setup_module, teardown_module, setup_function
    and teardown_function, methods named setup_class, teardown_class, setup_method and teardown_method, functions
    named test_ and classes named Test in files whose names mark them as tests; a program that reports unused code
    must not report them.
  example: a function named setup_module in a file named test_x.py is used, though nothing in the file calls it.
  stated:
  - nowhere: the test runner's own documentation is not kept in the language library.
